Limit: ACP1055-01: content carrying the binding marker is refused unless it is exactly one well-formed token; the marker matches any case and whitespace, dashes, underscores or nothing between acp, buzz and bind, after NFKC with format characters removed, so a message that merely names the marker is not delivered, and homoglyphs from other scripts are not folded
Ruled-out: reading content that is not exactly one well-formed token as an ordinary message | the parser's null sent `${token} ${token}` and a token beside a malformed prefix to both the peer and the owner paths (ACP1055-01); marker-carrying content is classified NONE, TOKEN or MALFORMED and only NONE reaches admission
Ruled-out: answering every replay of a consumed binding event as already applied | a refused write's replay became ALREADY_DURABLE and moved the subscriber's cursor past older undelivered owner messages (ACP1055-02); the writer's answer is kept beside the consuming event and only an accepted binding's replay is INGRESS_REPLAY_IGNORED
Warn: ACP1055-02: a consumed challenge keeps the writer's answer with its event; a refused write's replay returns that refusal and a write that threw is answered CONFLICT, both REFUSED, which moves no cursor; the nonce still never binds twice
Warn: the sink decides interception from the content, not from whether a challenge store is wired; with no store a marker-carrying message is refused outright, never delivered
Warn: r-0b16dd6d3a79's Warn that content carrying exactly one token goes to the binding was narrower than the behaviour after this commit: every marker-carrying message is kept from admission, and one that is not exactly one well-formed token is refused with INVALID_ARGUMENT and no audit row
